            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"5-why-it-was-wrong\">5. Why it was wrong</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">For each wrong answer, the fix usually lives in one of three places:</span>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The brief.</strong> Was the rule there? (e.g. \"missing is never zero\", \"say when a period isn't covered\".)</li>\n<li><strong>The layer.</strong> Did a column name or meaning mislead it? (e.g. a column called <code>score</code> with no period.)</li>\n<li><strong>The question.</strong> Was it ambiguous? Would a person have asked \"which year?\" first?</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Ask your AI:</strong> <em>\"My agent got this question wrong: [question]. Its SQL was [paste]. The known\nanswer is [answer]. In plain words, what did the query do differently, and what one line should I\nadd to the agent brief so it doesn't happen again?\"</em> Then rerun the question and record whether the\nfix worked.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Ask your AI:</strong> <em>\"Write five more test questions about this table [paste the column list] whose answer\nI can check myself, including one about a suppressed value and one about a reporting period.\"</em></span>\n</blockquote></span>"
          }
        }
